Know the diff, and remeber to use comparing not compare.
// 1. Using Comparator:  bookList.sort(Comparator.comparing((b -> b.author)));
// 2. Using Method reference: bookList.sort(Comparator.comparing(Book::getAuthor));
//3. Using Lmabda:   bookList.sort((b1, b2)-> b1.title.compareTo(b2.title));

Imp Mehtods:
Comparator.comparing,
Comparator.thenComparing

Here what it means, if author name is same, in that case the second comparison would be base on id, likewise.
comparing() is a static helper method introduced in Java 8.
Comparator<Book> idComp = Comparator.comparing(b -> b.getId());

