-------------------------------------------------------
Using replaceAll method, which have the return type:
studentNameMarksMap.replaceAll((key, value) -> {
                                            if (value < 35 & value >= 30) 
                                            { 
                                                value = value + (35 - value); 
                                                return value;
                                            } 
                                            return value;
                                            });

column8:
We can use Lambda expression in forEach and replaceAll method, the reason as below:
1. void forEach(BiConsumer<? super K, ? super V> action)
    @FunctionalInterface
      public interface BiConsumer<T, U> {
         void accept(T t, U u);
      }
    Exactly one abstract method → functional interface
    Therefore lambda => (key, value) -> System.out.println(key + " : " + value)

2. void replaceAll(BiFunction<? super K, ? super V, ? extends V> function)
     @FunctionalInterface
       public interface BiFunction<T, U, R> {
           R apply(T t, U u);
       }
 -> One abstract method → functional interface

In order to avoid concurrentHashMap Exception, you can use iterator, and directly perform operation on iterator.
Iterator<String> it = map.keySet().iterator();

       while(it.hasNext()){
        String str = it.next();
        if(map.get(str).isBefore(LocalDate.now())){
            it.remove();
        }
       }

